    ],
    "rewritten_article_markdown": "The idea of creating an official 'before and after' thread for Fullsize Chevrolet trucks and cars was proposed by GMCTruck21. The thread is meant to showcase the changes made to vehicles over time, providing a visual guide for those looking to modify their own trucks or cars.\n\nGMCTruck21 shared images of his 2002 GMC Sierra from March 1, 2010, and October 10, 2011. He stated that he wished the truck retained more of its original OEM style look: \n\n- *Before* (March 1, 2010): ![Truck on date of purchase](http://i275.photobucket.com/albums/jj286/Lukeizzle991/My%202002%20GMC%20Sierra/IMAGE_105.jpg)\n- *After* (October 10, 2011): ![Truck as of October 10, 2011](http://i275.photobucket.com/albums/jj286/Lukeizzle991/IMAG0774.jpg)\n\nOther members contributed their own 'before and after' projects. For instance, custm2500 suggested that the bumper and cap should be rino lined to match the rockers.\n\n- *Before*: ![Truck before modifications](http://i354.photobucket.com/albums/r418/Minimeh1993/96%20GMC%20pics/004.jpg)\n- *After*: ![Truck after modifications](http://i354.photobucket.com/albums/r418/Minimeh1993/IMG_0097.jpg), ![Truck after additional modifications](http://i354.photobucket.com/albums/r418/Minimeh1993/IMG_0100.jpg)\n\nAnother example was provided by probuilder1, who shared images of his truck before and after waxing:\n- *Before*: ![Probuilder1's truck before wax](http://i251.photobucket.com/albums/gg299/probuilder1/Truck.jpg)\n- *After*: ![Probuilder1's truck after wax](http://i251.photobucket.com/albums/gg299/probuilder1/waxed2.jpg)\n\nMembers also provided feedback, with GMCTruck21 praising probuilder1 for the result.\n",
