        "post_id": 3180,
        "rewritten_content": "Originally Posted by someotherguy\n\nYou're right; I must have misunderstood your previous post. The \"dumbo ears\" you mentioned were actually in the \"Before\" picture. I called them that because they provided adequate towing visibility without being overly large. While the large plastic mirrors are functional, since they were in high demand for my parts business, I sold a few to customers and used dumbo ears on the shop truck.\n\nThe cab lights are clear, not smoked; Recon offers both options. Clear lights matched the corners I chose. As for the chrome mirrors, some call them \"dumbo ears,\" but I think they look fine. I also wondered why 1988-1994 Ram 3500 models have that piece between the bumper and grill."
